      "text": "The script takes the value-weighted monthly block from the file and computes RMW as the average of the two High-OP portfolios (Small HiOP, Big HiOP) minus the average of the two Low-OP portfolios (Small LoOP, Big LoOP). Missing-value codes (-99.99, -999) become NaN, and months with any missing input are dropped.\n\n```python\nimport csv\nimport math\n\nIN_FILE = \"6_Portfolios_ME_OP_2x3.csv\"\nOUT_FILE = \"output.csv\"\nMISSING = {-99.99, -999.0}\n\n\ndef is_yyyymm(tok):\n    tok = tok.strip()\n    return len(tok) == 6 and tok.isdigit()\n\n\ndef parse_value(tok):\n    try:\n        v = float(tok.strip())\n    except ValueError:\n        return float(\"nan\")\n    if v in MISSING or v <= -99.98 and v >= -100.0 and abs(v + 99.99) < 1e-9:\n        return float(\"nan\")\n    return v\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(IN_FILE, \"r\", encoding=\"latin-1\", errors=\"replace\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    # Locate the value-weighted monthly block\n    start = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        if \"Value Weighted\" in line and \"Monthly\" in line:\n            start = i + 1\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        start = 0  # fallback: scan whole file for first YYYYMM block\n\n    rows = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines[start:]:\n        s = line.strip()\n        if not s:\n            if started:\n                break\n            continue\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in s.split(\",\")]\n        if is_yyyymm(parts[0]) and len(parts) >= 7:\n            started = True\n            date = int(parts[0])\n            vals = [parse_value(p) for p in parts[1:7]]\n            rows.append((date, vals))\n        else:\n            if started:\n                break  # end of monthly block (e.g., annual section or footer)\n\n    out = []\n    for date, v in rows:\n        small_lo, small_mid, small_hi, big_lo, big_mid, big_hi = v\n        r = 0.5 * (small_hi + big_hi) - 0.5 * (small_lo + big_lo)\n        if math.isnan(r):\n            continue\n        out.append((date, r))\n\n    with open(OUT_FILE, \"w\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        w = csv.writer(f)\n        w.writerow([\"date\", \"value\"])\n        for date, r in out:\n            w.writerow([date, repr(float(r))])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
